        "original_id": "1e79f173-06e4-53d3-9d44-9d0f85d385a2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John McPhun, Jairos Jiri\n- Places: Rhodesia, Salisbury, Harare, Southern Rhodesia\n- Sports: first-class cricket, Currie Cup\n- Topics: disability services, Christian charity\n\nFacts:\n- Southern Rhodesia achieved responsible government in 1923.\n- In the 1940s, Jairos Jiri began creating facilities in Rhodesia/Zimbabwe for disadvantaged and disabled people.\n- Jairos Jiri used Christian principles of charity, patience, and non-judgmental tolerance in this work.\n- John David McPhun was born on September 8, 1940, in Salisbury, Rhodesia.\n- John McPhun was a first-class cricketer who played for Rhodesia in the Currie Cup.\n- Rhodesia had its capital in Salisbury, now called Harare.\n- Rhodesia was considered a de facto successor state to the former British colony of Southern Rhodesia.",
